    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.32702v1</id>
    <title>CounselPlex: A Stressor-Aware Full-Duplex Counseling Model</title>
    <updated>2026-10-23T14:26:22Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.32702v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.32702v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Full-duplex speech models can listen and speak at the same time, enabling natural, low-latency interaction. In counseling, however, these models often focus on the latest utterance and lose track of the seeker's underlying problem. We call this failure Stressor Blindness. We propose CounselPlex, a stressor-aware full-duplex framework that uses two operations. CounselPlex updates a short stressor state during seeker silence and injects this state into &lt;PAD&gt; positions while listening. We also introduce RoPE Position Shift Augmentation (RPSA), which broadens positional coverage during training and improves performance at longer turn depths in our evaluation. LLM-judge evaluations show improved counseling quality and stressor grounding over strong baselines.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
